# ==============================================================================
# PortFusion — what git does NOT track
# The reasoning for each rule sits beside it.
#
# THIS LIST IS ALSO WHAT .githooks/pre-commit REFUSES. `git add -f` overrides an ignore rule
# and the hook does not, so adding a pattern here forbids committing it, not just forgetting it.
# ==============================================================================

# NO SPREADSHEET IS A SOURCE FILE. The record is the CSVs in store/, and a spreadsheet beside
# them would be a second copy of it in an opaque binary. The other two lines are the lock
# files LibreOffice and Excel leave beside an open copy.
*.xlsx
*.xlsx#
~$*.xlsx

# Python build cache, and the pytest cache beside it. Both regenerate on every
# run and carry no record. .pytest_cache/ added 26 Aug 2026, with the test suite.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch/intermediate files from mid-edit work. The proper restore point is a
# git commit, not a .bak copy left beside the original.
*.bak
*.tmp

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Credentials — nothing with an API key or a password ever enters this repo. .githooks/pre-commit
# holds it, down to a value pasted into some other file.
.env
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*

# IG session tokens, cached so one login serves a whole price run rather than one
# login per command, which would otherwise get the API key rate-limited.
# Listed separately because `credentials.*` does not match it, and it is every bit
# as sensitive: a CST and X-SECURITY-TOKEN are bearer credentials the full IG API
# accepts, dealing included, for up to 72 hours.
.ig_session.json
# TradingView's OAuth session — an access token and the refresh token that renews it. Bearer
# credentials to the TradingView account, alerts and watchlists included, for as long as
# the refresh token lives.
.tv_session.json
# The passkeys enrolled for the hosted desk (desk/auth.py). Public keys rather than secrets,
# but they say who may sign in, so they stay on the machine running the desk. With them, each
# reader's level and the sign-in log, whose addresses and times are nobody else's business.
.desk_passkeys.json
.desk_passkeys.tmp
.desk_readers.json
.desk_readers.tmp
.desk_signins.jsonl
.desk_signins.tmp
# The secret Netlify signs each proxied request with (desk/remote.py). A
# credential: whoever holds it can reach the door as if through the hosted page.
.desk_proxy_secret.json

# The intake workbench. Documents land in _inbox/ and LEAVE it: worked into store/, then
# moved to _archive/statements/, which IS tracked because it is the audit trail behind every
# figure. Contents are ignored here so a document is never committed under two paths, and so
# a half-worked intake cannot be mistaken for a record. The folder itself is tracked, via its
# .gitkeep — the workbench is part of the method, what sits on it is not.
# `.bench/` inside it, the desk's staging for an intake still being worked, is ignored with it.
#
# A document resting here is UNFINISHED WORK, and test_inbox.py says so.
_inbox/*
!_inbox/.gitkeep
# Its old guide, gone to docs/intake.md, is in past commits, which the history scan reads.
!_inbox/CLAUDE.md
# The demo book's workbench (PORTFUSION_BOOK=demo, record/schema.py), ignored as this one is. The
# other files a book keeps beside its store are ignored by the patterns above, wherever it is.
src/portfusion/demo/_inbox/

# The project virtual environment, added 1 Sep 2026 with the desk. Every byte of it is
# reconstructible from pyproject.toml and requirements.lock — which is the test for whether something
# belongs in git at all.
#
# LISTED EXPLICITLY ON PURPOSE. `python3 -m venv` drops its own .gitignore containing
# `*` inside the directory, so this was already ignored — by a file we do not own, that
# a different tool or a stray deletion would not recreate. Keeping the whole environment
# out of git should not rest on someone else's default.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH: `.venv/` matches a folder but not a link, and a venv may be either
# (docs/environment.md).
.venv

# Claude Code's own files. A clone carries no machine-level ignore, so they are listed here:
# otherwise the worktrees, whole checkouts of this repo, would go to the next `git add -A`.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# What pip writes into src/ when the checkout is installed: rebuilt by every install.
*.egg-info/

# What building a wheel leaves beside the checkout: the copy it packs, and the wheel.
build/
dist/
